ecks must be concrete, not generic \"looks good\". files must be the real touch-set / scheduler-allowed paths. workpack_touch_set and workpack_conflict_group are optional explicit scheduler metadata; omit them unless files alone would be ambiguous. Incomplete atoms are rejected by the deterministic ingest gate. IMPORTANT: every atom\u0027s \"chapter\" MUST begin with the plan chapter NUMBER it belongs to (the leading integer from the matching PROJECT_PLAN.md \"## ... N ...\" heading), e.g. \"Chapter 7 - Hardware triggers\". Decomposed-chapter progress is keyed on that ordinal, so a missing/inconsistent number makes the planner miscount and can skip or repeat a chapter.\r\n\r\nThe driver will add those atoms to approved project backlog automatically. Do not use operator-delegate and do not edit backlog.jsonl manually.\r\n\r\nFinish with STATUS: DONE after emitting the marker, or STATUS: DONE without the marker if no work remains.","after_turns":125,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":221.89,"success_pct":0.984},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-28T19:51:33.1735237Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"no_effect","ts":"2026-06-29T23:01:46.7849845Z","commit":"7be6e5ec114695339ee87d26d31b8d33e5888799"}
